.TH XCULL 1 "2026-05-27" "xcull 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
xcull \- security-aware URL deduplicator for recon pipelines
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B xcull
.RB [ \-F ]
.RB [ \-x ]
.RB [ \-a ]
.RB [ \-s ]
.RB [ \-k ]
.RB [ \-p ]
.RB [ \-W ]
.RB [ \-r ]
.RB [ \-V ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B xcull
reads URLs from standard input, one per line, and writes a deduplicated
set to standard output. It is built for the front of a bug-bounty or
penetration-test recon pipeline, where the input is the merged output
of crawlers and archive sources (gau, waybackurls, katana, hakrawler,
etc.) and the output is the working set passed to scanners, fuzzers,
and parameter miners.
.PP
The default policy is keep-biased and security-aware: every distinct
numeric, UUID, hex, and alphanumeric object identifier survives the
dedup, every distinct session token is preserved, and dedup is keyed
on the query parameter shape rather than the raw query string.
Templating, asset filtering, and wayback / scanner-probe noise removal
are on by default; each can be turned off by a flag.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-F
Fold object ids. Numeric, UUID, hex and stem-id segments collapse to
one witness per endpoint pattern. Default keeps every distinct id; use
.B \-F
for an aggressive route-discovery pass.
.TP
.B \-x
Keep invalid URLs, fully raw, no cleaning. The garbage gate is off; the
output is the raw structural dedup only.
.TP
.B \-a
Keep all assets. The render-noise filter is off, so
.IR .css ", " .png ", " .woff ", " .mp4 ", " .mp3 ", " .m4p
and the other binary media extensions are kept.
.TP
.B \-s
Case-sensitive path matching. Default folds path case so
.I /Login
and
.I /login
collide.
.TP
.B \-k
Keep parameter values and emit every distinct query key-set as its own
line. Disables the default query-subset merge and restores strict
streaming output.
.TP
.B \-p
No path templating at all. Also drops the title-slug fold, so
.I /blog/foo
and
.I /blog/bar
both survive.
.TP
.B \-W
Disable wayback noise handling. Scanner-probe URLs captured by archive
crawlers are kept verbatim.
.TP
.B \-r
Disable URL canonicalization. Percent-escapes, default ports, and the
other RFC 3986 normalisations are not applied.
.TP
.B \-V
Verbose mode. Writes
.I xcull: <in> -> <out>  (peak RSS <n> KB)
to standard error at end of run. Stdout still carries the URLs.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Clean recon surface from an archive feed:
.PP
.RS
.nf
gau example.com | xcull > surface.txt
.fi
.RE
.PP
Combine multiple sources and dedupe once:
.PP
.RS
.nf
cat gau.txt waybackurls.txt katana.txt | xcull | tee urls.txt
.fi
.RE
.PP
Feed a parameter-fuzzing pipeline:
.PP
.RS
.nf
gau example.com | xcull | qsreplace FUZZ | anew params.txt
.fi
.RE
.PP
Show the reduction (stats on stderr, data still on stdout):
.PP
.RS
.nf
cat urls.txt | xcull \-V > deduped.txt
.fi
.RE
.PP
Two passes: first preserve every IDOR-relevant id, then collapse them
for a route-scan witness set:
.PP
.RS
.nf
cat urls.txt | xcull        # default, /user/41 and /user/42 both survive
cat urls.txt | xcull \-F     # collapse to one route witness
.fi
.RE
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success. Non-zero on I/O error or out-of-memory.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR gau (1),
.BR waybackurls (1),
.BR katana (1),
.BR qsreplace (1),
.BR anew (1)
.PP
